  "run": {
    "id": "01M1NFS745PENPETBZSGV1H2YF",
    "status": "succeeded",
    "createdAt": "2026-09-04T05:55:35.174Z",
    "updatedAt": "2026-09-04T05:56:17.323Z",
    "errorMessage": null,
    "promptStatus": "completed",
    "headSha": "3747d90f79bd9bb3cd761e8f31d75e6d37156957"
  },
  "result": {
    "type": "trail_summary",
    "adapter": "markdown",
    "data": {
      "markdown": "**Problem:** The benchmark kit's adapters embedded hardcoded machine-specific paths (author's home directory) as defaults, making the kit runnable on only one machine and failing silently mid-ingest on others. Additionally, failed subprocess calls (binary missing, timeout, index error) were silently converted to empty results, making infrastructure failures indistinguishable from legitimate empty retrievals and skewing scores for the `entire` arm.\n\n**Solution:** Removed all machine-specific defaults from adapters (`cmm_client.py`, `graphify_client.py`). Replaced them with required environment variables (`CMM_BIN` defaults to bare name `codebase-memory-mcp` on `PATH`; `GRAPHIFY_PYTHON` and `GRAPHIFY_SOURCE` have no defaults and must be set). Added validation functions (`_resolve_binary`, `_require_configured_path`) that fail early at adapter construction with actionable error messages naming the variable to set—preventing opaque subprocess failures mid-run. Changed `entire_client.py` to raise `RuntimeError` on failed searches instead of returning `[]`, ensuring the harness's drop accounting treats infrastructure errors correctly. Improved logging to capture full stderr/stdout for diagnosis. Refactored unvendored backend loading to report missing adapter modules clearly rather than as `ModuleNotFoundError`. Added CI workflow and unit tests (`test_kit_reproducibility.py`, `test_kit_launcher_and_patches.py`) to guard portability, validate adapter configuration, verify patch integrity, and refuse `resume` mode for in-process buffered arms (`entire`, `graphify`, `cmm`, `bm25`). Updated launcher and documentation."
    }
  }
}

