    "createdAt": "2026-09-04T05:55:31.174Z",
    "updatedAt": "2026-09-07T19:36:24.53Z",
    "bodyDocument": {
      "textSnapshot": "Problem: The benchmark kit's adapters embedded hardcoded machine-specific paths (author's home directory) as defaults, making the kit runnable on only one machine and failing silently mid-ingest on others. Additionally, failed subprocess calls (binary missing, timeout, index error) were silently converted to empty results, making infrastructure failures indistinguishable from legitimate empty retrievals and skewing scores for the entire arm.\nSolution: Removed all machine-specific defaults from adapters (cmm_client.py, graphify_client.py). Replaced them with required environment variables (CMM_BIN defaults to bare name codebase-memory-mcp on PATH; GRAPHIFY_PYTHON and GRAPHIFY_SOURCE have no defaults and must be set). Added validation functions (_resolve_binary, _require_configured_path) that fail early at adapter construction with actionable error messages naming the variable to set—preventing opaque subprocess failures mid-run. Changed entire_client.py to raise RuntimeError on failed searches instead of returning [], ensuring the harness's drop accounting treats infrastructure errors correctly. Improved logging to capture full stderr/stdout for diagnosis. Refactored unvendored backend loading to report missing adapter modules clearly rather than as ModuleNotFoundError. Added CI workflow and unit tests (test_kit_reproducibility.py, test_kit_launcher_and_patches.py) to guard portability, validate adapter configuration, verify patch integrity, and refuse resume mode for in-process buffered arms (entire, graphify, cmm, bm25). Updated launcher and documentation.",
