trail-summary succeeded 51dfd917f605d0a14cee119315f1136b9a23ac48 {"type": "trail_summary", "adapter": "markdown", "data": {"markdown": "**Problem:**\n\nThe LoCoMo reproduction kit under `bench/memory/` had gaps in its guards against reproducibility issues. Adapter configurations could be non-portable, failed retrievals could be silently scored as empty results, the launcher could accept invalid resume modes, CMM binaries could be mismatched to their declared build, and patch consistency was unchecked.\n\n**Solution:**\n\nAdded comprehensive reproducibility guards across the benchmark kit:\n\n- New CI workflow (`bench-memory-kit.yml`) runs reproducibility tests on push and PRs, using only Python standard library so it cannot drift with dependency locks.\n- Updated adapter clients (`cmm_client.py`, `entire_client.py`, `graphify_client.py`) to validate adapter paths, gate construction on available factory options, and verify binary/source integrity.\n- Added `GRAPHIFY_SOURCE` checkout validation and CMM binary hash verification to match declared builds.\n- New test suite (`test_kit_reproducibility.py`) verifies adapter portability, proper error surfacing from failed retrievals, and FAIR-CONFIG hash consistency.\n- New launcher test suite (`test_kit_launcher_and_patches.py`) validates resume modes and patch integrity.\n- Updated `run_locomo.sh` with gated construction logic to make the kit runnable off the author's machine.\n- Refreshed FAIR-CONFIG MD5 hashes and trail 159 runner evaluations to reflect corrected builds.\n\nAll changes use pure standard-library Python to avoid dependency drift in CI guards."}}
"}

