    "updatedAt": "2026-09-07T19:41:18.828Z",
    "errorMessage": null,
    "promptStatus": "completed",
    "headSha": "51dfd917f605d0a14cee119315f1136b9a23ac48"
  },
  "result": {
    "type": "trail_semantic_diff",
    "adapter": "last_json_line",
    "data": {
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Binary and source verification guards",
          "summary": "Adapters now validate their configured engines at construction rather than failing opaquely mid-ingest, with CMM fingerprinting binaries to prevent scoring the wrong build and Graphify verifying both checkout structure and interpreter compatibility.",
          "sections": [
            {
              "files": [
                "bench/memory/benchmarks/common/cmm_client.py",
                "bench/memory/README.md",
                "bench/memory/FAIR-CONFIG.md"
              ],
              "title": "CMM binary fingerprinting and build verification",
              "description": "CMM_BIN is now required (no default), and the resolved binary is fingerprinted by scanning for BM25 exclusion-list string literals to identify stock vs patched builds. The fingerprint must match CMM_BUILD (default: 'patched') or construction aborts with CMM_UNPATCHED_BINARY, CMM_UNVERIFIED_BINARY, or mismatch errors. This prevents scoring the shipped v0.9.0 binary (which returns nothing on prose) under the published 'cmm (patched, Markdown-Section)' label."
            },
            {
              "files": [
                "bench/memory/benchmarks/common/graphify_client.py",
                "bench/memory/README.md"
              ],
              "title": "Graphify checkout and interpreter validation",
              "description": "GRAPHIFY_PYTHON and GRAPHIFY_SOURCE are now required (no defaults) and verified at construction. The source directory is checked for required entry points (graphify/extractors/markdown.py, graphify/serve.py with specific functions), and the selected interpreter is probed by running a test import of networkx and those modules. Either failure aborts before ingestion starts, replacing opaque mid-run subprocess errors with clear configuration messages."
            }
          ],
          "page_number": 1
        },
        {
          "title": "Adapter error propagation and factory changes",
          "summary": "Failed retrieval subprocesses now raise rather than return empty results, unvendored backends produce clear 'not included' errors instead of bare ModuleNotFoundError, and run metadata tracks CMM_BUILD.",
          "sections": [
            {
              "files": [
                "bench/memory/benchmarks/common/entire_client.py"
              ],
              "title": "Entire-graph search failures now raise",
              "description": "The entire adapter previously returned [] on subprocess failure (non-zero exit or non-JSON output), which bypassed harness retry/drop accounting and scored infrastructure errors as retrieval-quality misses. Now raises RuntimeError on both paths, matching cmm/graphify/bm25 invariant that a failed subprocess is not an empty retrieval."
            },
            {
              "files": [
                "bench/memory/benchmarks/common/entire_client.py"
              ],
              "title": "Unvendored backend loading and error messages",
              "description": "make_memory_client now uses _load_unvendored_client for cognee/graphiti/letta/supermemory, checking if the adapter module file exists before import and raising a clear 'not vendored in this kit' message if absent. A present module's own ImportError propagates unchanged so dependency problems are not misdescribed."
            },
            {
              "files": [
                "bench/memory/benchmarks/common/runmeta.py"
              ],
              "title": "Run metadata extended for CMM_BUILD",
              "description": "CMM_BUILD added to SYMMETRIC_ARM_SETTINGS and ENV_VALUE_DOMAINS (frozenset({'patched', 'stock'})) so implementation_provenance binds it and distinguishes the two builds' scores."
            }
          ],
          "page_number": 2
        },
        {
          "title": "Launcher guards and resume refusal",
          "summary": "run_locomo.sh now validates the selected arm against what the factory can construct and refuses resume for in-process buffered arms whose buffer would be empty on a resumed run.",
          "sections": [
            {
              "files": [
                "bench/memory/run_locomo.sh",
                "bench/memory/RUNNING-LOCOMO.md"
              ],
              "title": "Arm validation at launch",
              "description": "The launcher gates the arm argument against BUNDLED_ARMS and UNVENDORED_BACKENDS lists (kept in step with entire_client.py by ci/test_kit_launcher_and_patches.py). Unknown arms exit 5 immediately; unvendored arms without their adapter file exit 5 with a 'not vendored' message rather than constructing and dying inside make_memory_client."
            },
            {
              "files": [
                "bench/memory/run_locomo.sh",
                "bench/memory/README.md"
              ],
              "title": "Resume refusal for buffered arms",
              "description": "The launcher refuses 'resume' for entire/graphify/cmm/bm25 (IN_PROCESS_BUFFERED_ARMS) because they buffer ingestion in memory and materialize at first search, so a resumed run skips every add() and raises BUFFER_MISSING or scores a partial corpus. Exit 4 with explanation. Supplied adapters are heuristically checked for the same defect by grepping for 'BUFFER_MISSING'."
            }
          ],
          "page_number": 3
        },
        {
          "title": "CI and test coverage",
          "summary": "New CI job and 1110 lines of test coverage guard adapter portability, configuration validation, failed-subprocess propagation, and launcher/patch integrity.",
          "sections": [
            {
              "files": [
                ".github/workflows/bench-memory-kit.yml"
              ],
              "title": "bench-memory-kit workflow",
              "description": "New GitHub Actions workflow runs test_kit_reproducibility and test_kit_launcher_and_patches on push/PR. Pure standard-library (no deps install), tests that adapters refuse machine-specific defaults, verify CMM fingerprints match the patch, validate Graphify checkout structure, ensure failed subprocesses raise, and check that unvendored backends produce clear errors."
            },
            {
              "files": [
                "bench/memory/benchmarks/common/test_kit_reproducibility.py"
              ],
              "title": "Adapter reproducibility tests",
              "description": "838-line test suite covers: no adapter default points into /home or /Users, CMM fingerprints match stock/patched exclusion lists from patch 0005, resolved binaries are absolute, Graphify checkout/interpreter probes reject missing entry points or import failures, entire/graphify/cmm failed subprocesses raise, and unvendored backend selection produces kit-specific errors."
            },
            {
              "files": [
                "bench/memory/ci/test_kit_launcher_and_patches.py"
              ],
              "title": "Launcher and patch integrity tests",
              "description": "272-line suite validates run_locomo.sh arm lists match entire_client.py backend sets, unknown/missing/buffered arm refusals exit with correct codes, and every patch hunk header's line counts match its body (hand-edited hunks with stale counts break git apply)."
            }
          ],
          "page_number": 4
        },
        {
          "title": "Documentation and metadata updates",
          "summary": "README, FAIR-CONFIG, and RUNNING-LOCOMO updated to document required configuration, verification mechanics, code-hash manifest refreshed, and trail 159 evaluations regenerated.",
          "sections": [
            {
              "files": [
                "bench/memory/README.md",
                "bench/memory/FAIR-CONFIG.md",
                "bench/memory/RUNNING-LOCOMO.md"
              ],
              "title": "Configuration documentation",
              "description": "README now documents CMM_BIN (required) and CMM_BUILD, the binary fingerprinting table (patched/stock × CMM_BUILD setting → run/abort), GRAPHIFY_PYTHON/SOURCE requirements and verification steps, and the resume refusal for buffered arms. FAIR-CONFIG explains the fingerprinting rationale and updates code-hash manifest with new cmm_client.py and entire_client.py md5s."
            },
